# React Native's C++ build (ninja, cmake) cannot open a path longer than
# Windows' 260 characters, and pnpm's store directory names blow past it on
# their own: a native module lives under
#   node_modules/.pnpm/<name>@<version>_<every peer dependency and its version>/
# which for @react-native-community/netinfo came to 120 characters before the
# package's own path even began. The APK build failed on exactly that.
#
# Shortening those directory names fixes it at the source. The alternative —
# `node-linker=hoisted`, which Expo suggests for pnpm monorepos — was tried and
# reverted: it puts one React at the root for every package, and this workspace
# legitimately has two (the console's 19.2.8 and the one Expo SDK 57 pins,
# 19.2.3). Hoisting paired the console's react-dom with Expo's react, the
# dispatcher came back null, and fourteen console tests died in useState.
virtual-store-dir-max-length=40
